-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Flat Chain Step
-- statement:
--   **Every edge of the combined flat chain has its prescribed error.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let $\psi_{bi}$ be a bipartite state, and let `family` be an indexed polynomial family. Let $\gamma$ and $\zeta$ be errors, assume G-hat self-consistency with error $2\zeta$, and define
--
--   $$
--   \nu_3=138m\left(\gamma^{1/16}+\zeta^{1/16}+\left(\frac{d}{q}\right)^{1/16}\right).
--   $$
--
--   For every natural number $r$ and edge index $i$, the combined flat-chain error sequence $F_r$ satisfies $F_r(i)=2\zeta$ when $i<r$ and $F_r(i)=E_r(i-r)$ when $i\ge r$. Adjacent family members satisfy `SDDOpRel` with this error, stitching the recursive prefix to the post-move suffix.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_flatChainStep`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
